@startuml
title Selected Architecture A - current pilot and separately labeled future deployment
left to right direction
actor "Pilot user" as PU
node "CURRENT DESIGN: one desktop installation" {
  node "One Java 21 process / one Maven application" {
    component "Swing presentation" as SW
    component "Application + independent domain" as LOCAL
    component "SQLite / receipt adapters" as AD
    SW --> LOCAL : in-process use cases
    LOCAL --> AD : ports at runtime
  }
  database "Local SQLite file\nsource records + append-only postings" as SQLITE
  folder "Protected local receipts" as FILES
  AD --> SQLITE
  AD --> FILES
}
PU --> SW
package "FUTURE PRODUCT - not pilot deployment" {
  actor "Full-product user" as FU
  component "Primary web UI" as WEB
  component "Android / iOS\npossible later clients" as MOBILE
  node "Central application server" {
    component "Versioned HTTPS / server authentication" as API
    component "Reused application/domain\nserver authorization + transactions" as SERVER
    component "Server persistence / receipt adapters" as SA
    component "Notifications / Reporting / multi-step approval\nDEFERRED" as FUT
    API --> SERVER
    SERVER --> SA
    SERVER --> FUT
  }
  database "Central relational database\nchoice deferred; retain posting ledger" as CENTRAL
  folder "Private server receipt storage" as STORE
  cloud "Verification/reset + notice delivery\nchannel/operations to be specified" as DELIVERY
  FU --> WEB
  FU --> MOBILE
  WEB --> API : HTTPS
  MOBILE --> API : HTTPS
  SA --> CENTRAL
  SA --> STORE
  FUT --> DELIVERY
  SERVER --> DELIVERY : future account delivery
}
SQLITE ..> CENTRAL : future controlled import / reconciliation
FILES ..> STORE : future checked receipt migration
note bottom of SW
Local accounts and data authority only.
No pilot API/server/cross-device collaboration.
Swing does not satisfy CR-009 / FR-014.
end note
note bottom of API
Web acceptance requires a usable browser interface.
Server authority replaces local authority after controlled cutover.
No dual-write/offline synchronization implied.
end note
@enduml
